OL,3,GNEWSAReform Senedd motion declaring
OL,4,AWales should stay in UK voted down
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Senedd has narrowly rejected a
OL,7,FReform motion declaring Wales should
OL,8,Fremain part of the United Kingdom.
OL,10,FThe vote was initially tied, with 45
OL,11,Fmembers backing the motion and 45
OL,12,Fopposed, requiring Presiding Officer
OL,13,FHuw Irranca-Davies to cast the deciding
OL,14,Fvote against the proposal in line with
OL,15,Fparliamentary convention.
OL,17,FA Labour amendment, which sought to add
OL,18,Fthat "devolution is the settled will"
OL,19,Fof Wales offering "a better, more
OL,20,Fsecure and more prosperous future" than
OL,21,Findependence, was defeated by 82 votes
OL,22,Fto eight.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,434,430,260,140,0,100
